{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"The Virtuous Elephant: a past life story","html":"<article id='ja72'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Jātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Stories of Past Lives 72 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Varuṇavagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Warding Tree </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>2. Sīlavahatthijātaka </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Virtuous Elephant: a past life story </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Akataññussa posassa, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>An ungrateful person, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>niccaṁ vivaradassino; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>always looking for opportunity, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Sabbañce pathaviṁ dajjā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>even if given the whole earth, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>neva naṁ abhirādhaye”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>would still not be satisfied. </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Sīlavahatthijātakaṁ dutiyaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
